      "content": "Legitimacy for the defense often rests on the historical context of the Constitution and the perceived need to preserve the *federalist structure* of the US, not just the outcome of the vote. Proponents argue it is a deliberate anti-majoritarian feature to prevent the \"tyranny of the majority\" from dominating the nation politically.\n\nHowever, in the context of a 21st-century political party, you are correct that the \"protection of small states\" argument often functions more as a political defense for incumbent power rather than a strong constitutional defense for pure democratic fairness.",
